        "eyebrow": "Key Feature 04",
        "title": "Premium Build Without the Premium Price",
        "text_1": "The FLEX's steel frame with zinc alloy joints delivers the same commercial-grade durability found in reformers costing two to three times more. The 32 kg frame feels substantial and stable during vigorous exercise — no wobble, no flex, no sliding across the floor. The carriage glides smoothly on precision-engineered rails.",
        "text_2": "The black matte finish is a durable powder coating that resists sweat, scratches, and daily wear. The Your Reformer ($2,795) uses maple or walnut wood frames that are beautiful but bulky, heavy, and susceptible to humidity damage. The FLEX's steel-and-alloy construction is more durable, more stable, and costs less than half the price."
      }
