    "sp_qa": {
      "type": "sensol-product-qa",
      "blocks": {
        "qa_1": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does the FLEX differ from the FLEX AIR?",
            "answer": "The FLEX offers significantly more capability than the FLEX AIR: 90 kg maximum resistance vs 60 kg, dual 1000W servo motors vs 750W, and a more robust 32 kg frame vs 25 kg. The FLEX is designed for users who want more resistance range and training versatility, while the FLEX AIR is optimised for beginners and those who prioritise foldability and the lowest price point. The FLEX does not fold but offers a more substantial training experience."
          }
        },
        "qa_2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is 90 kg of resistance enough for advanced training?",
            "answer": "For the vast majority of Pilates and functional strength training, 90 kg is more than sufficient. Most traditional reformers with 5 springs provide approximately 60–75 kg of maximum resistance. The FLEX exceeds this range while offering the precision of 0.5 kg increments. If you're training for powerlifting or competitive Olympic lifting, you'll need a barbell setup. For everything else — Pilates, functional strength, rehabilitation, general fitness — 90 kg provides ample room for progressive overload."
          }
        },
        "qa_3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What are the three training modes, and how do I use them?",
            "answer": "Standard Mode provides traditional progressive resistance — ideal for building strength and endurance. Off-centre Mode shifts the resistance vector, forcing your stabiliser muscles to work harder and improving balance and coordination. Constant Mode maintains even tension throughout the entire range of motion, maximising time-under-tension — ideal for muscle endurance and rehabilitation. The Vesta Sensol App recommends which mode to use for each class, but you can also switch modes freely during any session."
          }
        },
        "qa_4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can the FLEX replace my gym membership?",
            "answer": "For many users, yes. The FLEX supports over 200 movements spanning Pilates, strength training, and rehabilitation. With the barbell bar and short handles, you can perform rows, presses, curls, extensions, and dozens of other strength exercises. The 90 kg resistance covers the training needs of most recreational exercisers. If your gym routine focuses on free-weight powerlifting at high loads, you'll still need a barbell. For everyone else, the FLEX is a genuine gym replacement — and it includes Pilates, which no gym offers on a reformer."
          }
        },
        "qa_5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does the FLEX compare to the Align-Pilates F3 Folding?",
            "answer": "The Align-Pilates F3 ($1,999) is a well-regarded spring-based reformer with an aluminium frame and foldable design. However, it lacks app connectivity, guided classes, precision resistance increments, adjustable training modes, and dual-function capability. The FLEX costs $799 less while offering significantly more features. The F3 is Pilates-only; the FLEX is Pilates plus strength training. The F3 has spring hooks; the FLEX has 0.5 kg digital increments. The F3 has one training mode; the FLEX has three."
          }
        },
        "qa_6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is the FLEX suitable for two people to share?",
            "answer": "Absolutely. The remote control and app make it easy to switch between personalised resistance settings in seconds. Each user can create their own profile in the Vesta Sensol App, which remembers their preferred resistance levels, training mode, and workout history. Many of our customers are couples who alternate between Pilates and strength sessions, or who train together with one doing Pilates while the other uses the strength training functions."
          }
        },
        "qa_7": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the warranty and return policy?",
            "answer": "The FLEX comes with a Lifetime Warranty on the frame and structural components, plus a 30-Day Money-Back Guarantee. If you're not completely satisfied within 30 days, return it for a full refund. Warranty claims are handled locally in Australia by Dute Fitness (Australia) Pty. Ltd. — no international shipping or long wait times."
          }
        },
        "qa_8": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How noisy is the servo motor?",
            "answer": "The FLEX's servo motors are designed for near-silent operation, producing only a gentle hum during resistance changes. In practice, the noise level is comparable to a quiet desk fan. This makes the FLEX suitable for apartment living, early-morning sessions, and late-night workouts without disturbing others. Spring-based reformers, by comparison, produce audible spring noise (creaking and clicking) during use."
          }
        },
        "qa_9": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does shipping take? Is it really free?",
            "answer": "Shipping is completely free to all Australian addresses. Standard delivery takes 3–7 business days to metro areas (Sydney, Melbourne, Brisbane, Perth, Adelaide) and 5–10 business days to regional areas. You'll receive tracking information via email once your order is dispatched."
          }
        },
        "qa_10": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What if I need more resistance later — can I upgrade?",
            "answer": "If you find yourself consistently training at the FLEX's 90 kg maximum and need more, the FLEX PRO ($1,800) offers 120 kg of resistance with a wider 0–145° arm range. Contact our support team at support@sensolfitness.com.au to discuss upgrade options and any available loyalty programmes for existing Sensol customers."
          }
        }
      },
